hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16513","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: Umm Kulthum daughter of Ali narrated to me, he said: I brought her a charity that had been ordered, she said: One of our foster children, for Maymun, or Mihran, the freed slave of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me that he passed by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to him: O Maymun, or O Mihran, indeed we are a household, we have been forbidden charity, and indeed our freed slaves are of ourselves, and we do not eat charity."
